[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n5_hugh"
text = "# DRAFT
# Prior Hugh at dusk, on the north walk (night 5, clear and cold). Grim; he means to see it ended tonight.
# (He arrests the porter at dawn. Nothing here says so.) He knows what happened in the chapter house. The blood on his
# sleeve (prior_sleeve): Wulfric's, and the porter was there first. Telling him what you've seen: Suspicion +10 (Ranulf overhears).
== start
(The prior is on the north walk, his tablet shut in his hand for once. He looks as if he hasn't slept.)
Hugh: Porter.
-> simon_dead [if died_simon]
-> simon_lived [if n5_saved=simon]
-> plain

== simon_dead
Hugh: A brother's throat cut on the chapter house floor, and the porter in the door. Thomas says you saved his life.
Hugh: Thomas is generous.
-> ended

== simon_lived
Hugh: Brother Simon says you pulled the man off him. He'll say nothing else. He shakes when I ask him.
-> ended

== plain
Hugh: Five nights since you came to that gate, and I've buried more brothers than in five years.
-> ended

== ended
Hugh: It ends tonight. One way or another, I'll have a name by Lauds.
-> topics

== again
(He's writing on his tablet again, and doesn't look up.)
Hugh: Go to your supper, porter.
-> topics

== topics
* [if prior_sleeve] [if not n5_hugh_sleeve] (Ask about the blood on his sleeve.) -> sleeve
* [if not n5_hugh_told] (Tell him what you've seen.) -> told
* [if not n5_hugh_means] (Ask what he means to do.) -> means

== sleeve [set n5_hugh_sleeve]
(He looks down at the sleeve. It's been scrubbed. The stain is still there.)
Hugh: Wulfric's. I knelt by him in the fog. You saw me do it.
Hugh: You were there before me, porter. You're always there before me.
-> topics

# Telling the prior anything: Suspicion +10, because Ranulf overhears (design doc).
== told [set n5_hugh_told] [suspicion 10]
(You tell him. He opens the tablet and writes until the wax is full.)
(Across the garth, someone moves out of the light and is gone.)
Hugh: I've heard you. Whether I believe you is another matter. Go and keep your gate.
-> topics

== means [set n5_hugh_means]
Hugh: What a prior is for. Find who has been killing my brothers, and see him taken.
Hugh: Keep to your gate tonight, porter. Keep to it, and I'll know where to find you.
-> topics

== leave
Hugh: Lauds, porter. I'll know by Lauds.
"
